cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "SEM Crack Detector"
abstract: >-
  A browser tool for detecting cracks in scanning-electron micrographs of steel and
  superalloy specimens, with a human-correction loop in which the reviewer's judgement
  always overrides the model and unreviewed pixels are never counted as negatives.
  Ships 62 annotated micrographs and 39 hand-drawn correction masks.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Jiaming
    # affiliation and orcid intentionally left blank -- fill these in before citing;
    # they are not inferred here because guessing an affiliation into a citation record
    # is the kind of error that propagates into other people's bibliographies.
repository-code: "https://github.com/jzhang29-max/sem-crack-detector"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
keywords:
  - scanning electron microscopy
  - crack detection
  - image segmentation
  - active learning
  - materials characterisation
references:
  - type: data
    title: "SEM Crack Detector: annotated SEM micrographs of cracking in 316H steel and cast/HIP superalloys"
    authors:
      - family-names: Zhang
        given-names: Jiaming
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    notes: >-
